  "caveats": [
    "WASM openDocument is Handle.openDocument after Node-side initSync — not browser first-paint. Browser adds WASM fetch+compile+instantiate time on cold page load.",
    "xlsx asymmetry: TS=full loadWorkbook; WASM=open_first_view + process_frame (lazy per-sheet parse; not identical work, especially at L/XL after #283)",
    "docx XL (xl_a.docx): TS oracle rejects word/document.xml > 25 MiB — BLOCKED for fair comparison. WASM opens the file; a one-sided WASM-only time is not useful. See draft issue.",
    "XL peak memory: peak-mem.mjs does not enumerate XL fixtures; xl_a.* rows show NOT_MEASURED. See draft issue.",
    "Save latency: not measured at M1 viewer stage — WASM save path not yet available. See draft issue.",
    "Node-only benchmarks (not browser first-paint / scroll / scroll-query); those metrics remain TODO(#8).",
    "Platform: Linux x86_64 CI box; results may differ on macOS/Apple Silicon. The spec gates perf in Chromium.",
    "Known-loss exceptions per Jared #30: xlsx S peak_mem, docx S/M peak_mem — stay LOSS with numbers; they are not gate-blocking.",
    "Perf gate is in REPORT MODE (PERF_GATE_MODE=report). WASM-beats-TS is tracked but not enforced. Jared sets PERF_GATE_MODE=enforce when READY (see #8)."
  ]
}
